---
import Variant from '../../layouts/Variant.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Variant
  title="ExCSV pack"
  description="Multi-table columnar ExCSV archive — .excsv.pack.zip and .extsv.pack.zip with manifest and per-column .col files."
  heading="Pack"
  lede="Column-oriented multi-table ZIP for wide tables, selective column reads, and database snapshots. Additive to plain and row-ZIP forms."
>
  <div class="format-card" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
    <span class="badge badge-stable">v0.3</span>
    <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0; color: var(--color-text);">
      Extensions: <code>.excsv.pack.zip</code>, <code>.extsv.pack.zip</code>.
      Spec: <a href="/spec/#pack-container">§11.5</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/boligolov/excsv/blob/main/docs/pack.md">docs/pack.md</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use pack</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Selective column reads</strong> — open one <code>.col</code> ZIP entry, skip the rest.</li>
    <li><strong>Better compression</strong> on homogeneous typed columns vs row-oriented ZIP.</li>
    <li><strong>Multi-table snapshots</strong> — orders + customers + products in one file.</li>
    <li><strong>Cheap append-column</strong> — add a <code>.col</code>, rewrite that table's <code>_header.excsv</code>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Not for row streaming or <code>awk</code>-over-unzip workflows — use <a href="/variants/plain/">plain</a> or <a href="/variants/zip/">row ZIP</a> instead.</p>

  <h2>Layout</h2>
  <p>Always manifest + table directories, even for a single table.</p>
  <pre><code>sales.excsv.pack.zip
├── _manifest.excsv          ← first ZIP entry, layout=pack
├── orders/
│   ├── _header.excsv        ← layout=columnar, rows=N
│   ├── 00-id.col
│   ├── 01-customer_id.col
│   └── 02-amount.col
├── customers/
│   ├── _header.excsv
│   └── ...
└── products/
    └── ...</code></pre>

  <h2>Manifest (<code>_manifest.excsv</code>)</h2>
  <p>Header-only ExCSV. Pack-only meta lines — never in plain files or table headers.</p>

  <CodeBlock title="Multi-table manifest" description="version=0.3 layout=pack">
{`#!excsv version=0.3 layout=pack table-count=3 original-size=3123200
#@pack-name: sales-q1-2026
#@source: warehouse-snapshot
#table name=orders    dir=orders/    columns=4 original-size=1843200
#table name=customers dir=customers/ columns=2 original-size=512000
#table name=products  dir=products/  columns=3 original-size=768000
#fk from=orders.customer_id to=customers.id
#fk from=orders.product_id  to=products.id`}
  </CodeBlock>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Header / meta</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>layout=pack</code></td><td>Required on manifest</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>original-size=</code></td><td>Sum of all <code>#table</code> column payload bytes</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>single-table=&lt;name&gt;</code></td><td>Optional default table for CLI; dropped when a second table is added</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>#table name= dir= columns= original-size=</code></td><td>Table registry</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>#fk from=t.c to=t.c</code></td><td>Informational foreign keys (no enforcement)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>ZIP comment <strong>SHOULD</strong> mirror the manifest for fast <code>info</code> / <code>table list</code> without decompressing columns.</p>

  <h2>Table directory</h2>
  <p>Each table: <code>_header.excsv</code> (schema + meta, no data rows) + column payloads (flat <code>.col</code> files or section folders).</p>

  <CodeBlock title="Table header" description="orders/_header.excsv — section-size enables chunking">
{`#!excsv version=0.3 layout=columnar rows=237000 section-size=10000 sql-dialect=postgres
#@source: sales_db.orders
#column name=id type=int unique=1
#column name=customer_id type=int
#column name=amount type=decimal unit=USD
#column name=note type=string
#%sum: ,,3854720.50,`}
  </CodeBlock>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Header field</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>layout=columnar</code></td><td>Required on every table <code>_header.excsv</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>rows=&lt;N&gt;</code></td><td>Authoritative row count</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>section-size=&lt;N&gt;</code></td><td>Rows per chunk; absent or <code>0</code> = one flat <code>.col</code> per column</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Column files (unsectioned)</h3>
  <p>When <code>section-size</code> is unset or <code>0</code>, each column is a single file:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Name: <code>&lt;index&gt;-&lt;safe_name&gt;.col</code> (e.g. <code>02-amount.col</code>; <code>header=0</code> → <code>&lt;index&gt;.col</code>).</li>
    <li>Contents: one value per line, plain text; empty line = empty field.</li>
    <li><code>wc -l</code> on the file <strong>MUST</strong> equal <code>rows</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <CodeBlock title="Flat column" description="orders/02-amount.col (excerpt)">
{`99.99
250.00
42.50`}
  </CodeBlock>

  <h3>Column chunking (sectioning)</h3>
  <p>
    When <code>section-size=&lt;N&gt;</code> is set, every column in that table is split into chunks of <code>N</code> rows.
    Each column becomes a <strong>folder</strong> named <code>&lt;index&gt;-&lt;safe_name&gt;/</code> containing section files
    <code>&lt;start&gt;.col</code> where <code>&lt;start&gt;</code> is the zero-padded starting row index (width scales with <code>rows</code>).
  </p>

  <pre><code>orders/                          ← section-size=10000 in _header.excsv
├── _header.excsv
├── 00-id/
│   ├── 000000.col                 ← rows 0..9999
│   ├── 010000.col                 ← rows 10000..19999
│   ├── ...
│   └── 230000.col                 ← rows 230000..236999 (short final chunk)
├── 01-customer_id/
│   ├── 000000.col
│   └── ...
└── 02-amount/
    └── ...</code></pre>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Shared boundaries</strong> — all columns in a table use the same section starts; only the last chunk may be shorter.</li>
    <li><strong>Row access</strong> — <code>section_start = (N / section_size) * section_size</code>; open <code>&lt;idx&gt;-&lt;name&gt;/&lt;section_start&gt;.col</code> and read line <code>N - section_start</code> (max scan <code>section_size - 1</code> lines).</li>
    <li><strong>Per-chunk Deflate</strong> — each chunk is its own ZIP entry with its own dictionary (better for low-cardinality columns and partial reads).</li>
    <li>Tables in one pack <strong>MAY</strong> use different <code>section-size</code> values (e.g. a small lookup table unsectioned, a fact table at 10k).</li>
  </ul>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th><code>section-size</code></th><th>Pro</th><th>Con</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Unset / 0</td><td>Simplest layout</td><td>O(rows) for any single-cell read</td></tr>
      <tr><td>1,000</td><td>Tiny in-chunk scans</td><td>Many ZIP entries</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>10,000</strong></td><td><strong>Recommended default</strong></td><td>—</td></tr>
      <tr><td>100,000+</td><td>Fewer entries</td><td>Slow scan inside a large chunk</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>CLI (target)</h2>
  <p><code>excsv [flags] PACKFILE &lt;command&gt;</code> — pack adds <code>--table &lt;name&gt;</code>. Not yet in <a href="/tools/">excsv-golang</a>.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Scope</th><th>Examples</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Pack</td><td><code>info</code>, <code>table list</code>, <code>fk list</code>, <code>meta list</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Table</td><td><code>rows --table orders</code>, <code>header list</code>, <code>sql list --verb ddl</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Column</td><td><code>col get amount --table orders</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Authoring</td><td><code>pack create</code>, <code>table add</code>, <code>table extract</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>vs row ZIP</h2>
  <p>
    Row <code>.excsv.zip</code> ships one inline table — unzip and pipe the data section.
    Pack trades that for column-selective I/O and multi-table bundles.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="/variants/zip/">Row ZIP</a> ·
    <a href="/spec/#pack-container">Spec §11.5</a> ·
    <a href="/variants/">All storage forms</a>
  </p>
</Variant>
